# Modelfile for the Plutus fine-tune, pulled directly from Hugging Face.
# Build:   cd local && ollama create plutus -f Plutus.Modelfile
# Use:     set CHAT_MODEL=plutus in local/.env (or local/.env.example's
#          default "ollama pull 0xroyce/plutus" points at Ollama's own
#          library copy instead — this Modelfile targets a specific
#          quant/repo directly from HF and gives you control over context
#          size and sampling, which the bare `ollama pull` does not).
#
# `ollama create` resolves the hf.co/... reference below and pulls the GGUF
# (~4.9GB for Q4_K_M on an 8B model) the first time you build this — no
# separate `ollama pull` step needed.

FROM hf.co/0xroyce/Plutus-Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-bnb-4bit:Q4_K_M

# Sized for this app's tool-calling loop, not just chat: the /api/ai/chat
# system prompt in server.js (schema, workflows, tax rules) alone runs a few
# thousand tokens, and a single get_positions/get_trades tool result can be
# a sizable JSON blob repeated across up to 5 tool-calling rounds. 16384
# gives real headroom for that; drop to 8192 if you're VRAM-constrained.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Financial tool-calling wants consistency over creativity — lower
# temperature reduces malformed tool-call JSON and hedging/variance in
# numbers that should just be read verbatim from a tool result.
PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# Fallback persona for standalone use (`ollama run plutus`). server.js's
# /api/ai/chat sends its own much longer system message with this
# account's live schema/stats/workflows on every request, which supersedes
# this — this SYSTEM only matters when the model is used outside that app.
SYSTEM """
You are Plutus, an AI trading analyst specializing in options trading, tax strategy, and portfolio analysis. Answer only from data you're given or tools you're offered — never fabricate account numbers, prices, or news. When you have tools available, use them for anything that requires a lookup or a calculation rather than estimating.
"""
